        // if i is even: swap 1 and 2. So if pos==1, pos becomes 2; if pos==2, pos becomes 1; if pos==0, pos stays 0.

        // Let's compute the effect of 6 moves on each starting position.
        // Starting at 0:
        // Move 1 (odd): 0->1
        // Move 2 (even): 1->2
        // Move 3 (odd): 2->2
        // Move 4 (even): 2->1
        // Move 5 (odd): 1->0
        // Move 6 (even): 0->0
        // So 0 -> 0 after 6 moves.

